      "side": 1,
      "message": "I haven\u0027t dived into the code but keep in mind that `MemoryTracker` (and in particular this code) was written for pvmfw, which runs _outside_ of the main memory region unlike guest kernels such as Rialto.\n\nTherefore, this method probably doesn\u0027t check for clashes between `region` and the running image from Rialto (the entries of which are created in `new_page_table`) and is, in some way, broken for Rialto asi t  could overwrite parts of \"itself\" by (unknowingly) mapping something over its own address ranges.\n\nIn general, I believe that this issue and what this CL is achieving should be addressed by re-architecting/generalizing the code to cover them both instead of adding \"special cases\" like `alloc_range_outside_main_memory` does but this can be considered a clean-up and doesn\u0027t have to block this CL; @alanstokes@google.com, WDYT?",
